{"chunk_id": "51595251996f", "text": "Rama watches Sugriva falter in his duel with the mighty monkey king Bali and finally intervenes. From concealment he releases a thunderous arrow that pierces Bali\u2019s chest, felling the seemingly invincible warrior like Indra\u2019s banner struck down. Yet Bali does not immediately die; protected by a divine golden necklace, he lies radiant even in defeat. As Rama and Lakshmana approach, Bali rebukes Rama in a fierce moral challenge. He condemns the hidden attack as unworthy of a righteous king and accuses Rama of disguising injustice beneath virtue. Bali argues that Rama violated the code of warriors and kings, and even claims that, had Rama asked openly, he himself could have captured Ravana and recovered Sita. The episode is pivotal because it introduces a profound ethical debate about dharma, justice, and the legitimacy of Rama\u2019s actions.\nRama secretly shoots Bali during his duel with Sugriva; the wounded Bali condemns Rama\u2019s conduct as unrighteous and deceitful.\nThemes: justice and dharma, war ethics, betrayal and reproach, heroic downfall, fate and counsel ignored", "vector": [-0.007121581584215164, -0.023140039294958115, -0.0035335831344127655, -0.00027717711054719985, -0.008944489061832428, 0.008379931561648846, -0.03371017798781395, -0.02024243213236332, -0.03120708279311657, -0.025398267433047295, 0.006227132398635149, 0.004346409346908331, 0.0009386611636728048, 0.0014955661026760936, -0.01593003235757351, 0.011263933964073658, 0.051476724445819855, -0.010386490263044834, 0.03286674618721008, -0.013889464549720287, -0.002824485767632723, -0.0001923660165630281, -0.00023530297039542347, 0.012563095428049564, -0.014732899144291878, 0.006682859268039465, 0.028921646997332573, -0.03145195171236992, 0.01451523881405592, -0.026758644729852676, -0.004400824662297964, -0.018623581156134605, -0.004298795945942402, 0.0058394246734678745, -0.03327485918998718, 0.003489370923489332, -0.0038362673949450254, -0.00729